{"title":"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the product of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real\">real</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Root\">roots</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Equation\" title=\"Equation\">equation</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec154f9fe04cdb60993633cbd9e8d1c47138298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 18x + 30 = 2 \\sqrt{x^2 + 18x + 45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"267\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d69f90d156a30a909aaa98ce31e8d523d79dcae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2+18x+30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />. Substituting into the original equation yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84bb3150bc7abbd1833ee104536662484914981b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2\\sqrt{y+15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"112\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>Squaring both sides yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/9/ce99f05bbdb23069189c525df7d980938fa04389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 = 4y + 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, which can be rearranged to form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc83a88a1384c92dba340b36b7e3de1356ad22ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 - 4y - 60 = (y-10)(y+6) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"277\" height=\"21\" />.  Though this quadratic has roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/3683f227b0b53e6a30087db2fa3b752965ecf05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3beb254e4896c351752e5b3da7096049bce6d21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> satisfies the original equation.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e53d9d1bea7ea78e97249c67c57127be4816e59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2+18x+30=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"20\" />, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf926f9e058a71e359610d5caf9ae2af2c304fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+18x+20=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />.  This quadratic has discriminant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/8/d380c2154afac5cb7a10f08eab3b6f0943a63ab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 20 = 244 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />, so both its roots are real. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_Formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s Formulas\">Vieta's Formulas</a>, the product of these roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b15fcf701ef3c4c9bca88d5da9948166d6027b00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by noticing that the polynomial on the left is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> less than the polynomial under the radical sign. Thus: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d1386afb9df223b99ba60fac9a605075cb8c84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^2+ 18x + 45) - 2\\sqrt{x^2+18x+45} - 15 = 0.\\]\" width=\"354\" height=\"21\" /> Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/6303c77e3b449687d591f98bc867e32b972d957f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\sqrt{x^2+18x+45}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f21976d6fb34aecc535326eae335912665de96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-2n-15 = 0 \\Longrightarrow (n-5)(n+3) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"319\" height=\"19\" />. Because the square root of a real number can't be negative, the only possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Substituting that in, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b947673e88af58758c22d33f18075eafda05e7fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{x^2+18x+45} = 5 \\Longrightarrow x^2 + 18x + 45 = 25 \\Longrightarrow x^2+18x+20=0.\\]\" width=\"500\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Reasoning as in Solution 1, the product of the roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b15fcf701ef3c4c9bca88d5da9948166d6027b00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Begin by completing the square on both sides of the equation, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f2f3734cd292880a6327c8d916304540672faa4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+9)^2-51=2\\sqrt{(x+3)(x+15)}\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"32\" />\nNow by substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c4321eddef8604a06dab3dc88166cc7e35fa25d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74d9ca7faef322caec33290680ca15825d0b655c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-51=2\\sqrt{(y-6)(y+6)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"219\" height=\"32\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d9a5531c3ca6ff4740254ca25a2703f38aa4a5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^4-106y^2+2745=0\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />\nThe solutions in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/2/7a251c6a0e08f8d8fd2c36ea6f2f06fbb2a26ad0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=x+9=\\pm3\\sqrt{5},\\pm\\sqrt{61}\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"20\" />\nTurns out, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0df2ebabbb730f636dd339c02632cff712c119e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm3\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> are a pair of extraneous solutions. Thus, our answer is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8f66bbfa33c114c79df3b7b40aa4301a92b2e7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\sqrt{61}-9\\right)\\left(-\\sqrt{61}-9\\right)=81-61=\\boxed{020}\\]\" width=\"332\" height=\"32\" />\nBy difference of squares.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df9fe13e0626e179af81061d87d5e0e22179e6c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+18x+30=2\\sqrt{x^2+18x+45}\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />\nSquaring both sides yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301e0bbecfbd8042ff209d2a40d6bf21aa3c5a6c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^2+18x+30)^2=4(x^2+18x+45)\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/1517eb794bf756235eeaf88df6685eddc812b332.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^2+18x+30)^2=4(x^2+18x+30+15)\\]\" width=\"324\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a48b6514eba61e3cc2ef1bf345fd09936003b5cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^2+18x+30)^2=4(x^2+18x+30)+60\\]\" width=\"325\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe80497979920c45ebd5e845a5acdd0cc342458c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^2+18x+30)^2-4(x^2+18x+30)-60=0\\]\" width=\"357\" height=\"19\" />\nSubstituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d69f90d156a30a909aaa98ce31e8d523d79dcae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2+18x+30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /> yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/9/db9aa692ed69eae58c6394ff2fa6974142695d7a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^2-4y-60=0\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86e59d72b37413bf2c08d6d2dd7eb7da01fb677.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(y+6)(y-10)=0\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/0830fa4c17ee2db56c5f7748cd88385757089c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2+18x+30=-6,10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" />. However if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a6f8dc90670a02c1ee3f61d17da8f5e6e19d705.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />, the left side of the equation \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df9fe13e0626e179af81061d87d5e0e22179e6c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+18x+30=2\\sqrt{x^2+18x+45}\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />\nwould be negative while the right side is negative. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3beb254e4896c351752e5b3da7096049bce6d21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> is the only possible value and we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2ccfc8237ee5609edbb3c08d876f90f164fc16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+18x+30=10\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58f10046fff604f594d89e7357007c21741cdae6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+18x+20=0\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />\nSince the discriminant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/2/682b4d10f667477d83b6256555becfa0e4fac4ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{18^2-4\\cdot20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> is real, both the roots are real. Thus by Vieta's Formulas, the product of the roots is the constant, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b15fcf701ef3c4c9bca88d5da9948166d6027b00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~ Nafer\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME\" title=\"1983 AIME\">1983 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174245\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 300/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1431/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8057/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.542      1 Template:AIME_box\n100.00%    7.542      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2760:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174245 and revision id 273076. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}